  "body": "[2.4.5.4 Times](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#times) defines the concept of [time](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-time) as follows:\r\n\r\n> A time consists of a specific time with no time-zone information, consisting of an hour, a minute, a second, and a fraction of a second.\r\n\r\nBut the last part, “a fraction of a second” never seems to be used. The way the specification defines time to be parsed always returns the time consisting of three parts ([parse a time string](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parse-a-time-string) step 5):\r\n\r\n> Let time be the time with hour hour, minute minute, and second second.\r\n\r\nThe use of “hour hour, minute minute, and second second” repeats for several parser definitions. Never is “fraction of a second” used by any parser definitions.\r\n\r\nIs there any reason to keep fraction of a second separated from just second? Would there be a better way to just define second as not always being an integer?",
